## Notes for me

### how to create CSV for DB file

1) "Export Filtered CSV" for PKM and MTG => Exclude "Unopened" condition
2) Open files independently in spreadsheet tool and remove: 1) title column 2) all columns after "Condition"
3) Manually merge both files in a text editing tool -- taking care not to include the headers twice -- and save as new CSV.

### how to create sqlite DB

```
sqlite3 mydatabase.db
.mode csv
.import filename.csv tablename
.quit
```

If you're creating this DB file yourself, you need to know the following:

* I called the file `catalog.db` _and_ the table `catalog`
* Columns are: "TCGplayer Id", "Product Line", "Set Name", "Product Name", "Number", "Rarity", "Condition"
* These map to the same columns in CSV Exports from the `Pricing Tool` 

